# ── injishi (app, mobile, web, api, packages) ────────────────────────────────
# Pure application code, plus the committed packages/ source. Nothing else.

# ── Context / AI docs: HARD BLOCK ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The documentation corpus lives in injishi.context and is published from there.
# The workspace root owns the single CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md pair — no per-package
# copies, at any depth. `tools/guard-splits.mjs` fails the publish on a leak.
dox/
docs-context/
.context/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.windsurfrules
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.claude/
.claude.json

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER add a bare `dist/` rule here. `packages/design-tokens/dist/` is a build
# output committed ON PURPOSE — it is what `apps/mobile` and the CSS emitter
# read, and `pnpm -F @injishi/design-tokens check` fails when it drifts from
# `src/`. `packages/{auth,contracts}/dist/` are still the only copy of those two
# until ADR-034 task 8 reconstructs their source. Every rule below is scoped to a
# workspace directory so packages/ is never swept up.
apps/*/dist/
apps/*/.next/
# `.next-prod` is a second Next build directory (`next build --distDir`), and it
# was NOT covered by the rule above. 530 of its files reached the initial commit,
# two webpack packs among them at 148 MB and 127 MB, and GitHub refused the push
# (GH001, 100 MB ceiling). Keep both spellings.
apps/*/.next-prod/
apps/*/.next-build/
# `.next-verify` and `.next-verify2` are the same story a third and fourth time:
# a `--distDir` build made to check something without disturbing the running dev
# server's `.next`. 131 of their files reached a commit on 2026-09-05 before it
# was undone. Any `.next-*` sibling is build output; match the whole family
# rather than adding a line per spelling.
apps/*/.next-*/
apps/*/.turbo/
apps/*/.expo/
# `apps/mobile` carries its Expo cache one level deeper than the rule above
# reaches, so `devices.json` and the generated router types kept showing up as
# untracked. Match `.expo/` at any depth under `apps/`.
apps/**/.expo/
apps/*/out/
# `storybook build` output (ADR-045). Scoped to the one package that runs it.
packages/ui/storybook-static/

# Serwist compiles `apps/web/src/app/sw.ts` into `public/sw.js` on every build.
# It is output, not source, and it was tracked by mistake: a stale copy in the
# tree shadowed the real one and made the service worker look unchanged when it
# was not. The source it is built from stays tracked.
apps/web/public/sw.js
apps/web/public/sw.js.map
apps/*/build/
server/*/dist/
# `worker:dev` builds into its own folder so it can run beside `api:dev`,
# whose watcher deletes dist/ on every start (demo-comms).
server/*/dist-worker/
server/*/.turbo/
server/*/build/
tools/*/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Turborepo's task cache, at the root and in every member.
.turbo/
# Next.js 16 rewrites this on every `next dev` and `next build` (with a
# different types path for each), so a tracked copy is always dirty.
next-env.d.ts
# Expo's generated native projects, and `expo export` output: `dist-android`,
# `dist-web` and every per-persona copy of them (`dist-web-staff`, ...).
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/dist-*/

# ── Embedded dev database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @injishi/db's libSQL/SQLite file, re-seeded from @injishi/data fixtures.
.data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HeroUI Pro tokens live only in .env.local (or a CI secret), never in .npmrc.
# Env files (2026-10-24, root .env.example): everything with a secret stays out
# of git. Committed are the examples, the local test stack's file (made-up
# local values), and the apps' development files (local addresses only).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!server/api/.env.test
!apps/*/.env.development
.npmrc.local

# ── Logs / coverage / test output ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
coverage/
# A route folder, not a test coverage report.
!apps/app/src/app/(workspace)/admin/leaders/coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.gstack/
# unlazy's local gate and hook state.
.unlazy/
.unlazy-hook-state.json

# Local object storage (F-S09 seam, ADR-026). `LocalDiskStorageAdapter` writes
# uploaded certificates here in development. These are real personal documents
# in every sense that matters; they must never reach a commit.
.storage/

.vercel
